# THE SUITE REGISTRY — every contract suite in this repo, and who runs it.
#
# Format:  <directory>  <harness>
#
# Harnesses:
#   contract-runner           the vendored Haskell Gherkin executor. We are the
#                             PROVIDER: legs 0, 1, 2 and 4 all apply, so its
#                             expectations are executed against the recorded pact.
#   contract-runner-consumer  the same executor, but we are the CONSUMER: these
#                             are our expectations of somebody else's API, which
#                             they run against their own server. Held to totality,
#                             vocabulary and semver here; never executed here,
#                             because we are not the provider and their server is
#                             not ours to start.
#   aqc-dual                  the Atlas Query Contract's own dual harness --
#                             Rust `cucumber` in-process (server/atlas-server/
#                             tests/aqc_cucumber.rs) AND C# Reqnroll
#                             (client.ContractTests). NOT executed by the Haskell
#                             runner: its steps are defined in those two harnesses,
#                             and its corpus uses Gherkin constructs (Scenario
#                             Outline) the vendored parser does not implement.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (fix round 1, review C-2).
#
# The gate used to name its suites in a literal bash array, which is how
# `contracts/atlas-edge` came to be excluded from every tag check -- a one-line
# `@target` could disarm map-generator's expectations of us and nothing objected.
# The fix was to enumerate from the filesystem so nothing could escape. But the
# filesystem alone cannot say WHICH executor owns a suite, and pointing the
# Haskell runner at the AQC corpus produces a wall of "undefined step" reds for a
# suite that is perfectly healthy under its own harness -- caught by
# scripts/gate-selftest.sh on its first run, not by inspection.
#
# So detection stays with the filesystem and classification lives here, and the
# gate FAILS on any suite it finds that this file does not list. Adding a suite
# without registering it is therefore impossible to do quietly, which is the
# property the literal array lacked.

contracts/atlas-graph-contract   contract-runner
contracts/atlas-edge             contract-runner
contracts/map-api-consumer       contract-runner-consumer
contracts/atlas-query-contract   aqc-dual
